# ***Data Dives: Simplifying Analysis and Prioritizing Action***

BuildingBlocks brings your city's property data into one place, so you can move from scattered records to clear priorities. Here's how to get the most out of it, one step at a time.

### ***Combine Your Data***

Frequent code violations, a recent police call, and a utility shutoff can each point to a property that needs attention. When all three show up at the same address, that property should move to the top of the list.

BuildingBlocks lets you view and filter data from across departments to find and sort the properties that need attention, all within minutes.

### ***Score for Prioritization***

Once you've identified the properties to focus on, the next step is deciding which ones come first. Use BuildingBlocks to build custom scores around your current initiatives, available resources, and capacity to act, so your team's time goes where the need is greatest.

### ***Monitor Neighborhood Health***

With a live view of the events affecting each property, and a score that ranks them across multiple factors, you can step back and assess the overall condition of entire neighborhoods, zip codes, or districts.

### ***In Practice: Buffalo, NY***

The City of Buffalo uses BuildingBlocks to measure neighborhood needs by combining event and condition indicators into a custom score. That score helps their team decide which communities to prioritize in ongoing cleanup efforts. [Read the Buffalo case study](/blog/case-studies/city-of-buffalo-ny).

Want more tips on getting the most out of BuildingBlocks? [Reach out to our team](mailto:support@tolemi.com) and we'll walk you through it.
